.TH MYSTRFUNCTIONS 3 "September 2026" "libmyutils 1.0" "libmyutils Manual"
.SH NAME
mystrlen, mystrcpy, mystrncpy, mystrcat \- custom string manipulation functions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "mystrfunctions.h"
.sp
.BI "int mystrlen(const char *" s ");"
.br
.BI "int mystrcpy(char *" dest ", const char *" src ");"
.br
.BI "int mystrncpy(char *" dest ", const char *" src ", int " n ");"
.br
.BI "int mystrcat(char *" dest ", const char *" src ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
These functions provide custom implementations of common C string operations, similar in spirit to the standard C library's string.h functions.
.PP
.B mystrlen
returns the number of characters in the null-terminated string
.I s,
not counting the terminating null byte.
.PP
.B mystrcpy
copies the null-terminated string
.I src
into
.I dest,
including the terminating null byte, and returns the number of characters copied.
.PP
.B mystrncpy
copies at most
.I n
characters from
.I src
into
.I dest.
If
.I src
is shorter than
.I n,
the remainder of
.I dest
is padded with null bytes. Returns the number of characters actually copied from
.I src.
.PP
.B mystrcat
appends the null-terminated string
.I src
to the end of the null-terminated string
.I dest,
and returns the new total length of
.I dest.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.B mystrlen
returns the length of the string.
.B mystrcpy,
.B mystrncpy,
and
.B mystrcat
return the number of characters written or copied.
